    "title": "Appalachia deserves access to justice - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Emily Hall ,\n15 hours ago This article was published as part of The New Political's 2026 Spring print. Equal access to justice is a foundational principle of our legal system, yet for many rural Ohioans, their access to legal representation is often uncertain. Across Appalachian counties, residents are facing a shortage of practicing attorneys and fewer legal resources than those who live in urban areas. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
